# **Hypothesis.** Blood volume and blood lost stay within a few mL of the 0.02 s run at 0.04 and 0.08 s, and MAP and heart rate at 5 min within 1 mmHg and 2.5 /min, while per-second samples of MAP and heart rate scatter more the larger the step. 0.04 s runs about twice as fast and 0.08 s about three times.

